Fastlane metadata for Open Circuits Android.

## Screenshot capture

Screenshots are stored in metadata/android/en-US/images/phoneScreenshots/.
They should be taken on a Pixel 6 emulator (API 35, 1080x2400) with airplane
mode ON to confirm offline operation.

To regenerate:

1. Start a Pixel 6 emulator via Android Studio or:
     avdmanager create avd -n pixel6 -k "system-images;android-35;default;x86_64" \
       --device "pixel_6"
     emulator -avd pixel6 -no-audio -no-window -gpu swiftshader_indirect &

2. Enable airplane mode on the emulator:
     adb shell cmd connectivity airplane-mode enable

3. Install the debug APK:
     ./gradlew :app:assembleFossDebug
     adb install app/build/outputs/apk/foss/debug/app-foss-debug.apk

4. Launch and take screenshots:
     adb shell am start -n org.hearth.circuits/.MainActivity
     # Navigate to desired screen, then:
     adb exec-out screencap -p > fastlane/metadata/android/en-US/images/phoneScreenshots/1.png
     # Repeat for screens 2-4

Recommended screens:
  1.png  Home / table of contents
  2.png  Chapter mid-scroll (DC_1 or similar)
  3.png  Search results
  4.png  Settings popover open

## Feature graphic

featureGraphic.png must be exactly 1024x500. To regenerate with ImageMagick:
    convert -size 1024x500 xc:'#F6F3EB' \
      -fill '#935F16' \
      -draw "rectangle 0,0 1024,48" \
      -draw "rectangle 0,492 1024,500" \
      -font DejaVu-Sans-Bold -pointsize 48 \
      -fill '#935F16' -gravity center \
      -annotate 0 'Open Circuits' \
      fastlane/metadata/android/en-US/images/featureGraphic.png
